Summary
Bella Haire is a growing solo-founder e-commerce business selling standard and made-to-order hair products. I am looking for an experienced operations systems architect and automation builder who can first design the right process architecture and then implement a practical, maintainable system.

This is not a request for a few isolated automations. I need one connected operating system and daily dashboard that reduces manual work, prevents information from getting lost, and clearly shows what needs attention.

The system must support:

• CRM, leads, follow-up and complete customer history
• Consultations, fittings and appointments
• Shopify orders and manually entered made-to-order orders
• Deposits, outstanding balances and payment status
• TO ORDER items and factory purchase orders
• Supplier/Erica workflow, approvals and version/change control
• A unique record and status history for every individual wig
• Production, quality control, shipping and delivery
• Inventory and stock availability
• Klaviyo customer journeys and transactional communication
• Aftercare, issues, returns and resolutions
• Costs, landed cost, revenue and margin visibility
• A daily dashboard showing exceptions, overdue actions and priorities

Current and preferred tools include Shopify, HubSpot, Klaviyo, Calendly and Make or n8n. APIs or light custom development may be used where necessary, but I do not want an unnecessarily complex custom platform.

PHASE 1 — DISCOVERY AND ARCHITECTURE

• Map the complete current and future workflow
• Identify the source of truth for every important record and status
• Design the data model, lifecycle stages, ownership rules and exception handling
• Recommend what should remain in Shopify, HubSpot and Klaviyo
• Propose a phased implementation plan with priorities and estimated effort

PHASE 2 — BUILD AND IMPLEMENTATION

• Configure the agreed system
• Build and test integrations and automations
• Create the operational dashboard
• Handle manual overrides, duplicate prevention, error alerts and retry logic
• Document the system and provide a clear handover

THE IDEAL FREELANCER

• Has personally designed and built complete operational systems, not only individual automations
• Understands e-commerce operations, orders, purchasing, inventory, production and customer lifecycle management
• Has hands-on experience with Shopify, HubSpot, Klaviyo and Make or n8n
• Can translate messy real-world processes into a simple, reliable system
• Is willing to challenge unnecessary complexity
• Can work independently with a solo founder and communicate clearly
• Can show comparable work and explain what they personally designed and built

PLEASE ANSWER IN YOUR PROPOSAL

1. Describe the most comparable operational system you personally designed and built.
2. Which system would you use as the source of truth for customers, orders, individual made-to-order items, supplier purchase orders and inventory, and why?
3. How would you prevent duplicates, missed updates, and conflicts between manual changes and automations?
4. What would you include in phase one, and what would you intentionally postpone?
5. Share a relevant dashboard, workflow or case study and explain exactly what you built.
6. Which parts would you solve with existing tools, and when would you recommend custom development?

Please do not propose a large custom application before first understanding and mapping the business process.